<div id="how-forecasts-are-made">
  <details>
    <summary class="p-3">
      <h2 class="h2 mb-1">How the forecasts are created</h2>
    </summary>
    <div class="text-block p-3">
      <p>Forecasting is complex and airTEXT brings together data from several world-renowned systems to give the most accurate forecasts we can.</p>
      <p>airTEXT brings together air quality forecasts using the <%= link_to 'air pollution forecasting system from CERC', 'https://www.cerc.co.uk/forecasting.html', target: '_blank' %>.</p>
      <p>It brings in information from weather forecasts, forecasts of pollution across Europe from the <%= link_to 'CAMS Regional Ensemble', 'https://atmosphere.copernicus.eu/', target: '_blank' %> and detailed data from 30,000 pollution sources across London are fed into the <%= link_to 'ADMS-Urban air quality model', 'https://www.cerc.co.uk/environmental-software/ADMS-Urban-model.html', target: '_blank' %> to produce the forecasts.</p>
      <p>Real-time monitoring data from <%= link_to 'LondonAir', 'https://www.londonair.org.uk/LondonAir/Default.aspx', target: '_blank' %> is fed in throughout the day and these are compared with observed pollution levels to ensure accuracy. </p>
      <p>The hourly concentrations of four pollutants are calculated:</p>
      <ul class="bullets">
        <li>Nitrogen Dioxide (NO<sub>2</sub>)</li>
        <li>Particulates (PM<sub>10</sub> and PM<sub>2.5</sub>)</li>
        <li>Ozone (O<sub>3</sub>)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>From the hourly concentrations the daily air quality index (DAQI) of each pollutant is derived. The overall air quality index is determined by the highest index for any of these pollutants.</p>
      <p>Forecasts are issued twice a day at 7am and 7pm. airTEXT issues an alert for a local authority or region if at least 10% of the geographical area is predicted to reach moderate or above.</p>
      <p>It also includes ultraviolet (UV) and temperature forecast information <%= link_to 'supplied by DTN', 'https://www.dtn.com/weather/', target: '_blank' %> and <%= link_to 'pollen forecast information', 'https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/weather/warnings-and-advice/seasonal-advice/pollen-forecast', target: '_blank' %> supplied by the Met Office.</p>
    </div>
  </details>
</div>
